SQLite is in the public domain.

From https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html: "All of the code and documentation in SQLite
has been dedicated to the public domain by the authors. ... Anyone is free to copy, modify,
publish, use, compile, sell, or distribute the original SQLite code, either in source code
form or as a compiled binary, for any purpose, commercial or non-commercial, and by any
means."

The library here is built by vendor/fetch.py from SQLite's own amalgamation (sqlite3.c),
unchanged.
